\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Rock of Ages, cleft for me,
\par Let me hide myself in Thee;
\par Let the water and the blood;
\par From Thy riven side which flowed,
\par Be of sin the double cure,
\par Cleanse me from its guilt and power.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Not the labours of my hands
\par Can fulfil Thy law's demands;
\par Could my zeal no respite know,
\par Could my tears for ever flow,
\par All for sin could not atone:
\par Thou must save, and Thou alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Nothing in my hand I bring,
\par Simply to Thy Cross I cling;
\par Naked, come to Thee for dress;
\par Helpless, look to Thee for grace;
\par Foul, I to the fountain fly;
\par Wash me, Saviour, or I die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. While I draw this fleeting breath,
\par When my eyelids close in death,
\par When I soar to worlds unknown,
\par See Thee on Thy judgement throne:
\par Rock of Ages, cleft for me,
\par Let me hide myself in Thee.
\par                                  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

